Not quite—pull and push are used to send and receive files via ADB, but in Git, those terms mean something completely different.
Because you used both tools, it is easy to mix them up! Here is the direct breakdown of how the terms change depending on the tool you are using:
## 1. In ADB (Phone to Computer)
You are moving physical files between your Android phone and your Ubuntu machine.

* adb pull: Copies a file/folder from the phone to your computer (like when you grabbed the APK).
* adb push: Copies a file/folder from your computer to the phone.

## 2. In Git (Computer to GitHub/Cloud)
You are syncing code history and tracking changes between your local Ubuntu folder and a remote cloud platform (like GitHub or GitLab).

* git pull: Fetches and merges code history from the cloud repository down to your computer.
* git push: Sends your committed local history changes from your computer up to the cloud repository.

